{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792273903,"nonce":"0qROKSy0acGrNlFY2PzIzFDw2AY=","title":"Python: deltablue's constraint lists are dynamic, and its loop is mostly boxing","message":"deltablue runs about 1.4x PyPy per iteration on the Mac (0.30 ms against 0.23 ms). Its loop samples are `zyntax_alloc` 31%, `zyntax_free` 6% and `memmove` 8%; the allocations are mostly instance boxes (`zb_hook_box_instance`, `zb_box_instance`) and dynamic list boxes and copies (`zb_list_box_any`, `zb_list_copy_any`). `Variable.constraints`, `Plan.v` and the planner's `todo`/`sources` lists are `List(Object)`, and `execute`, `output`, `satisfy`, `is_satisfied`, `recalculate` and `inputs_known` are opened as called on unknown receivers.\n\nFixed here, each needed on the way:\n\n- `class OrderedCollection(list): pass` made `OrderedCollection()` a `list()` call, which was typed `List(Object)` at once rather than by what the program appends. Sugar now rewrites `list()` to `[]` (unless a module binding shadows `list`).\n- A local bound to a followed field (`cc = v.constraints`) is followed as the field in list-site analysis instead of keeping it.\n- The kinds written into a list join through `join_classes`, so an `EditConstraint` and a `Constraint` give a list of `Constraint`.\n- Reading a field that only some subclasses define, through a receiver typed as the base, dispatches on the class instead of being refused (more precise list typing reached this in `class/explicit_base_call`).\n\nStill open:\n\n- `Variable.constraints` decides `List(Constraint)` in `field_lists`, but `denest` widens it to `List(Object)` because the field is also read through a dynamic receiver. That receiver is `v` in `add_constraints_consuming_to(v, coll)`, which is `Object` because the `todo` list it came from is: a cycle.\n- `make_plan(sources)` does `todo = sources`, aliasing a parameter. Following a name alias the way fields are followed broke lowering (a typed list reached a callee whose parameter had become `Object`, and `coll.append` raised AttributeError), so it was backed out. The aliasing has to be modelled in both inference and lowering.\n\nSuite total 0.999 with deltablue 0.902; all kernels check.","files":null}]}